    "narrative": "The primary engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is undoubtedly **Corbin Carroll**, who leads the lineup with a stellar 77.88 efficiency score. While he faces Michael McGreevy, whose 4.53 xERA provides a target-rich environment, **Corbin Carroll** gains significant utility from his #3 spot in the order and a favorable platoon matchup. Following him, **Josh Naylor** (65.03) serves as our most reliable anchor in the utility slot; his consistent ability to drive runs against Chandler makes him an essential start, despite the moderate pitcher profile. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Tyler Soderstrom** also offer strong value, hovering in the high-50s and low-60s, as both capitalize on mid-tier pitching matchups that allow their offensive upside to shine in the heart of our order.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles, specifically the uncertainty regarding the lineup submissions for **Max Muncy**, **Jose Caballero**, and **James Wood**. **Jose Caballero** remains a high-interest start (59.98) due to the substantial platoon advantage against Connelly Early, effectively offsetting his lower spot in the lineup. Conversely, **James Wood** (51.16) is a high-variance play; while his elite xwOBA and lead-off status keep him in the mix, he faces a daunting test against Cristopher S\u00e1nchez, whose 2.84 xERA is the most restrictive on the board today. **Cole Young** represents our most difficult decision, landing at 43.10; while he lacks the explosive potential of others, he stays active to keep the offense balanced, as our deeper options like **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Carson Williams** are currently shelved in favor of the current active configuration. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the current health of the roster. With **Trevor Story** continuing his stint on the IL and several key contributors like **Brice Turang** and **Mickey Moniak** sitting out due to off-days, our bench depth is intentionally thin. We are monitoring **Max Muncy** closely; his projection of 45.43 is borderline, and if his \"Lineup Pending\" status shifts him even further down the order, he risks falling below our 40-point efficiency floor. As we chase the league's scarcest category in stolen bases, we are prioritizing the mobility of **Corbin Carroll** and the utility of **Jose Caballero** to ensure we maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 sprint.",
